					<h1 class="title" title="Bhiwadi - Growing Industrial City">Bhiwadi - Growing Industrial City</h1>
<div class="entry-content">
<h3>Background</h3>
<p><b>Bhiwadi</b> is an Industrial town located in <b>Tijara Tehsil</b> of <b>Alwar district in Rajasthan, India</b>. It has been able to establish 
itself among the <b>fastest-growing cities of India</b>. What makes Bhiwadi a compelling proposition is its 
close proximity with <b>Delhi</b>, which in turn, has earned it the sobriquet of a <b>`Regional Center’</b> or 
Priority Town of the <b>National Capital Region (NCR)</b>. </p>

<h3>How to reach here</h3>
<p>Bhiwadi is just 55 km away from the <b>Indira Gandhi International Airport, New Delhi</b>, 200 km from 
<b>Jaipur</b>, 90 km from <b>Alwar</b>, 40 km from <b>Gurgoan</b>, and 5 km from <b>NH-8</b> (Delhi- Jaipur 
highway) on the <b>Dharuhera- Sohna road</b>. </p>

<h3>Economic Development and Business</h3>
<p>Bhiwadi being located next to Gurgaon & <b>Manesar</b> has a close proximity to the Northern and Western 
<b>markets of India</b>. It is emerging as a prime choice for limitless business opportunities. It has 
thousands of small, big and mid-sized industries of steel, furnace, electronics, engineering, textiles, 
pharmaceuticals, printing, cables, rolling mills, food processing, herbal care etc. All these industries are 
represented by <b>BMA</b> (<b>Bhiwadi Manufacturing Association</b>).

<p>Bhiwadi sub-region is playing a major role in the <b>economic development of Rajasthan</b> and has 
metamorphed into <b>3rd largest industrial centre of India</b> from last few years...more or less the credit 
goes somewhat to the top notch company establishments such as Pepsi, Honda Siel, Orient Craft, Asahi, Hero 
Honda, Bausch & Lomb, United Breweries, Ray Ban, Saint Gobain, Gillette and SEZ of Mahindra and Mahindra. All 
the major business tycoons either have established or in the process of establishing at least one unit here. 
The over all infrastructural development is generating a liberal number of <b>employment opportunities for 
youth</b>. The <b>Rajasthan Housing Board</b> has contributed immensely by creating the necessary 
infrastructure by way of schools, hospitals, banks, transportation, water supply and telecommunications 
networks. It is a well planned <b>industrial township</b> of Rajasthan.</p>

<p>From being a flourishing industrial town, it is fast becoming a preferred haven for real estate developers 
as good investment option. The future enormous opportunities in the real estate, retail and hospitality 
industries inspired many famed builders to sense the housing needs of the people & are developing state of art townships with modernized facilities.</p>

<h3>Places to Visit</h3>
<p>Bhiwadi being a fastest growing city does not have much tourist attractions but <strong>Vijay Mandir Palace</strong> 
constructed in 1918 by Maharaja Jai Singh and a well-laid garden and rippling lake in front is worth watching. 
Other major attractions around Bhiwadi are <strong>Sita Ram temple, Jaisamand Lake</strong> and 
<strong>Siliserh Lake</strong> and palace built by Maharaja Vinay Singh.</p>


